Review written to `docs/reviews/equipment-hvac/equip-hvac-02-boiler-hydronic-loop-integration.md` (81 lines, 5 findings).

**Summary of findings:**

| # | Severity | Issue |
|---|----------|-------|
| 1 | **High** | Boiler delivers heat to both Fluid port AND zone Thermal port simultaneously, but no terminal-unit model exists to transfer heat from the fluid loop to the zone. The hydronic water mass contributes zero thermal capacitance to the zone energy balance. |
| 2 | **Medium** | Default return temp of 40 °C (104 °F) is applied to both condensing AND non-condensing boilers. With non-condensing outlet of 82 °C, the 42 °C delta-T far exceeds the typical 11 °C (20 °F) design delta-T. |
| 3 | **Medium** | `supply_temp_c` is computed from heat balance but never clamped to the boiler's design outlet temperature, allowing supply temps outside physical boiler limits. |
| 4 | **Low** | Default flow rate of 0.5 kg/s lacks specific source citation and is oversized for most residential boilers. |
| 5 | **Low** | `DuctConfig` is applied to boiler configs, allowing duct DSE to silently reduce hydronic boiler output if configured. |
